{"benchmark": "livebench_selected", "task_id": "paraphrase:91b1079c3dd6f0c003bb20f34f3783141cbc55926e6e3001ba18eaba3acc169e", "sample_idx": 16, "model_name": "qwen/qwen3-next-80b-a3b-instruct", "content": "\"skill in solving sudoku puzzles often hinges on logic and patience, much like navigating the complex weight of climate policy decisions. While the grid demands precision with numbers 1 to 9, real-world challenges require balancing competing interests — each number, like each policy, must appear once and only once to maintain equilibrium.\n\n\\n\\n\n\nThe temporary nature of quick fixes in climate strategy mirrors the fleeting satisfaction of guessing a cell without full analysis. Just as relying on a single gas-powered solution to curb emissions may offer short-term relief, it undermines the integrity of the broader system. True progress requires methodical, holistic approaches — not shortcuts.\n\n\\n\\n\n\nA sudden twist in the puzzle — a misplaced digit — can unravel hours of work, just as a political twist or corporate scandal can derail climate initiatives. Whether in logic grids or global governance, one error can cascade, reminding us that every choice carries ripple effects across interconnected systems.\n\n\\n\\n\n\nThe weight of responsibility falls on those who commit to the full process — not those seeking the easy solution. In both sudoku and sustainability, the reward lies not in the final answer alone, but in the disciplined journey to reach it — where every row, column, and box, like every sector and community, must hold its rightful place.\"", "logprobs": [{"token": "\"", "logprob": -2.4437606043647975e-05}, {"token": "skill", "logprob": -0.0016066036187112331}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -0.02808956988155842}, {"token": " solving", "logprob": -0.015920665115118027}, {"token": " sudoku", "logprob": -0.970703125}, {"token": " puzzles", "logprob": -0.1790037751197815}, {"token": " often", "logprob": -1.82247793674469}, {"token": " hinges", "logpro